    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, and welcome. I'm Dr. [Name], a psychiatrist. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Well, hello Doctor. I came in because... gosh, I just feel like I cannot settle inside my own skin anymore. It's like this awful feeling where I have to jump up and do the next thing, even when I am completely worn out and I really should just be sitting still. \n\nLike yesterday, I tried to just sit down and watch my stories—I've been watching *General Hospital* since I was in high school, and let me tell you, the storylines lately are just ridiculous. Sonny is always in some kind of trouble, I don't know how he gets away with it. But anyway, I couldn't even sit through a whole scene. I got up to fix a crooked picture frame in the hallway, and then I saw a smudge on the glass, which reminded me I needed to buy paper towels. The prices at the grocery store right now are just highway robbery, by the way. I went to get a carton of eggs last week and nearly had a heart attack right there in aisle four. The young man working the register didn't even know how to bag the groceries right, put my bread right under a giant bottle of laundry detergent. \n\nBut yes, I just... I can't seem to stay sitting down, even when my bones are tired.",
